</tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>2. Undo the nuts (2a) and the bolts (2b) fixing the crankcase sump.</p><p>3. Use the tool to cut the crankcase sump sealant.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Blade</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.870.718.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>4. Remove the crankcase sump.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2043900.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[4,1,0,"<p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428938\">1072C16</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428939\">1072C44</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428915\">1048A10</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Connect the negative (-) battery terminal.</p><p>Refill the engine oil lubrication system \n\n                                          <a href=\"#/2428822\">0010T11</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Remove the car from the ramps.</p>"],[8,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Clean any sealant residues from the matching\nsurfaces between the lower engine crankcase and the crankcase sump.</p><p>1. Apply a bead of recommended silicon sealant to the contact surfaces\nof the crankcase sump and the lower engine crankcase as illustrated\nin the diagram below.</p><p>N. A: There should not be any breaks in the sealant bead. The diameter\nof the sealant bead should be 3.5 0.5. mm</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001236.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Type</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Qty.</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Sealant</p></td><td><p>OIL SUMP</p></td><td><p>LOCTITE 5900</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>-</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2052473.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Thoroughly clean the contact surfaces of\ncrankcase sump and cylinder block of sealant residues.</p><p>Apply silicon sealant around the edge of\nthe crankcase sump.</p><p>1. Refit the crankcase sump</p><p>2. Tighten nuts (2a) and bolts (2b) securing the engine block to\nthe recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2a</p></td><td><p>Nut</p></td><td><p>OIL SUMP</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>OIL SUMP</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1</p></td></tr></table></div><p>3. Tighten the engine oil drain plug to the specified torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>-</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2043901.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[8,1,0,"<p>1. Place the crankcase sump (1a) back in its housing and secure\nit by tightening the bolts (1b) and the nuts (1c) to the recommended\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>OIL SUMP</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Lower engine crankcase side) 0.8 ÷ 1.0</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1c</p></td><td><p>Nut</p></td><td><p>OIL SUMP</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Timing cover side) 0.8 ÷ 1.0</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2052474.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,1,0,"<p>1. Refit in its seating the bracket between the manual gearbox/engine\n(1a) and tighten the bolts (1b) to the specified torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>-</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2043902.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[8,1,0,"<p>1. Tighten the crankcase sump drain plug to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>ENGINE OIL DRAIN PLUG</p></td><td><p>M14</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Crankcase sump side) 1.8 ÷ 2.2</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2052475.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,1,0,"<p>Proceed with the refitting  \n                                          <a href=\"#/2429109\">2110A10</a></p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428938\">1072C16</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428939\">1072C44</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/2428915\">1048A10</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/2429401\">5530B52</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                                          <a href=\"#/2429398\">5530B10</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Proceed with refitting \n                          